    "created_at": "2024-01-08T21:52:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-08T21:52:31Z",
    "body": "> I'm playing with Declarative shadow dom and found that, if a stylesheet is loaded inside a declarative shadow DOM template, the rendering is blocked. Safari (that also implement declarative shadow DOM) however does not block rendering, which causes a FOUC.\r\n\r\nI think this is likely just inadvertent behavior in Chromium. Having said that, it does sound like a nice bit of behavior, to avoid the FOUC issue as you mentioned. I'd be supportive of a spec change to make that the official behavior.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
