    "created_at": "2024-07-11T16:25:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-07-11T16:25:03Z",
    "body": "Spec'ing this to match Chrome's behaviour, or providing a way to achieve this behaviour, seems essential for declarative shadow DOM.\r\n\r\n- Declarative shadow DOM exists so custom elements can render in some meaningful way before JS loads, and to avoid a layout shift when JS loads.\r\n- Custom elements typically need styles within their shadow root to achieve their desired layout.\r\n- Outputting inline styles per instance of a component would massively and needlessly bloat the HTML.\r\n\r\nThat means we want some way to include styles in the shadow roots:\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<custom-whatever>\r\n  <template shadowrootmode=\"open\">\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"custom-whatever-styles.css\" />\r\n    …\r\n  </template>\r\n  …\r\n</custom-whatever>\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut, if `<custom-whatever>`'s content renders before `custom-whatever-styles.css` loads, it's missing the whole point of avoiding a layout shift.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
